  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n\"On platforms where Esc is the [close request](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#close-request), the user agent will first fire an appropriately-initialized [keydown](https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-keydown) and [keyup](https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-keyup) event sequence\" example is rather confusing when step 4 above explicitly talks about picking up keydown. And keydown/up happen often (always?) in different tasks.",
